{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets (excl. territories) and the 2025 population from the census file's own 'United States' row : how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786911748809},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to calculate farmers markets per 100,000 residents using:\n1. A dataset with total farmers markets (excluding territories): https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\n2. 2025 population from the census file's 'United States' row: https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\n\nAccording to the AGENTS.md instructions, I should:\n1. **Orient first** - check `xorq_semantic_models` and `xorq_catalog_list_aliases` to see if the data already exists in the catalog\n2. If not, I need to ingest both sources as separate aliases first\n3. Then create a derived metric that joins them and calculates the ratio\n4. Use `xorq_select` to get the final number\n5. Use `xorq_verify` to verify it with an obligation\n6. Use `xorq_check_lineage` to verify the sources\n\nLet me start by checking what's in the catalog.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you calculate the farmers markets per 100,000 residents. Let me start by checking what's already in the catalog."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01ABCPowqFoazT4dYqEEtYSt","name":"xorq_catalog_info","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_014rsxgZyyZn21YrZux8ZXBM","name":"xorq_semantic_m